      "content": "hey, i've been looking at some orbital resonance data and the density calculations for the moon just don't add up. when you run the mass-to-volume ratio against the seismic data from the Apollo missions, the numbers suggest the interior is way less dense than a solid silicate body should be. basically, it looks like the mass is concentrated heavily in a thin outer shell. i'm trying to model the structural integrity of what this would look like if the core was actually hollow or metallic. can you help me work through the gravimetric equations for a shell-based mass distribution? i think i'm missing a variable for the internal cavity pressure.",
